<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What Android's backup and device transfer carry, decided rather than inherited (Phase 5,
  owner's request; docs/adr/0007-backup.md).

  Without this file the platform backs up everything the app owns, which is the default and
  not a choice. Passo's data is worth carrying: the step history is the one thing a new phone
  cannot rebuild. So an allowlist:

  - the database (`passo.db` and its write-ahead log): the steps minute by minute, the daily
    summaries, the tracker state and the log. The tracker state describes one phone's counter
    and would be wrong on another; it travels with the rest because it cannot be cut out of
    the file, and the service drops it on the first start of an installation that did not
    write it (`TrackingRepository.adoptTrackerState`), so the first sample there is a
    baseline, as on a first run.
  - `files/datastore/settings.preferences_pb`: the profile, the goal, the settings, and the
    installation the tracker state belongs to, which is what makes that check possible.

  Left out by not being named: the widgets' looks (keyed by widget ids, which a restore
  renews), caches, and `no_backup`.

  The same list twice on purpose: `<cloud-backup>` is the copy Android sends to Google Drive,
  end-to-end encrypted with the phone's PIN, pattern or password since Android 9, and only if
  the reader turned backup on; `<device-transfer>` is the direct phone-to-phone move. Passo
  sends neither itself and needs no permission for them: Android does the moving.

  NOT `android:allowBackup="false"`: on Android 12 and later some makers' phones still move the
  app's data in a device transfer anyway. An instruction whose effect depends on who made the
  phone is not a decision (Chiaro's reasoning, the same here).
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <include domain="database" path="passo.db" />
        <include domain="database" path="passo.db-wal" />
        <include domain="file" path="datastore/settings.preferences_pb" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <include domain="database" path="passo.db" />
        <include domain="database" path="passo.db-wal" />
        <include domain="file" path="datastore/settings.preferences_pb" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
